# PART 4: MAKE VITRAX AI FAST AND RESPONSIVE

The current application sometimes takes too long to answer.

Perform a genuine performance audit.

Inspect the entire request lifecycle from message submission to the final rendered response.

Identify unnecessary latency caused by duplicate requests, excessive prompts, repeated context, unnecessary multi-model calls, blocking operations or inefficient rendering.

## 4.1 Intelligent request handling

Use the following principles:

- Stream responses whenever supported by the configured provider.
- Use a single appropriate model for ordinary questions.
- Avoid repeatedly sending irrelevant conversation history.
- Use parallel requests only when tasks are independent and parallel execution improves the result.
- Reserve additional verification and multi-stage analysis for complex tasks.
- Cache safe, reusable results where appropriate.
- Use sensible request timeouts.
- Support cancellation.
- Prevent duplicate message submissions.
- Make retries bounded and deliberate.
- Keep completed work when a subsequent operation fails.
- Use background jobs for genuinely long-running document or coding tasks where the architecture supports them.

Show useful progress indicators for longer tasks.

Never display a permanently running indicator after the request has ended.

The stop button must cancel the actual supported operation and disappear after completion.

Do not sacrifice answer quality simply to make the application appear faster. Optimise the underlying workflow.

Measure response latency and failure rates where possible. Do not claim a performance improvement without evidence.

